    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to disclosures by limited licensees",
    "basePrintNo": "S5747",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5747-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2131, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5747\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn  act  to  amend  the  insurance  law, in relation to disclosures by\nlimited licensees\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo clarify the disclosure  requirements  for  wireless  communications\nequipment insurance companies.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThe  bill  amends  section  2131  which  sets  forth the requirements,\nincluding disclosures, of limited licensees which can offer  insurance\nfor wireless communications equipment.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe  wireless communications vendor (\"wireless vendor\") is licensed as\na \"limited licensee\" under Section  2131  of  the  Insurance  Law.  As\nrequired  under  §2131(e)  (2),  when  the  wireless vendor offers the\npurchaser  of  wireless  communications  equipment   the   option   of\npurchasing  wireless  communications equipment insurance, the wireless\nvendor makes available to the purchaser written materials  summarizing\nthe  material  terms of the insurance. coverage, including the name of\nthe insurer and the  agent  licensed  under  section  2103(b)  of  the\nInsurance Law. Additionally, such materials indicate that this product\nmay  be  a  duplication  of  coverage  already provided by a renter's,\nhomeowner's,  automobile,   or   other   liability   insurance.   This\ntransaction  occurs  at  a  kiosk  or  electronics  store in which the\nconsumer may purchase wireless communication equipment. The  materials\nand  disclosures  required  to  be  provided to the consumer here were\ntailored in statute to fit into this unique transaction.\n\nThe information necessary to affect whether or  not  to  purchase  the\ncoverage  is  presented  to  the  consumer by the wireless vendor is a\nunique transaction in which only one insurance product is offered, and\nthe consumer only had to decide whether or not to include the  product\nwith their purchase of the wireless device. The consumer does not have\nto  weigh  competing  products  or  coverage levels. They need to know\nterms,  cost,  and  procedure,  all  of  which  is  provided  in   the\ndisclosures required in §2131.\n\nThe  disclosures  provided  in the current law have been identified as\nnecessary and comprehensive for this type of transaction.\n\nThis fast, convenient transaction would be burdened with  a  stack  of\nmaterials   required   to  be  given  to  consumers  yet  lacking  any\ninformation that would benefit them or assist them in making  the  one\ndecision they make, whether, or not to purchase the one insurance plan\noffered  with  their  wireless  communication  device. Thus, this bill\nassures that the  current  set  of  disclosures  required  of  limited\nlicensees  contains the information necessary for the consumer to make\ntheir decision  and  continues  the  ample  and  specifically  devised\ndisclosure  and  consider  protection already existent in §2131 of the\nInsurance Law.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
